# Create a file with spaces
touch "my important file.txt"

# WRONG - tries to delete "my", "important", and "file.txt"
file="my important file.txt"
rm $file
# BREAKS!

# CORRECT - deletes the single file
rm "$file"

-----------------------

Example:
hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main [?]
➜ touch "my important file.txt"

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main [?]
➜ ls
'my important file.txt'   notes

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main [?]
➜ file="my important file.txt"

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main [?]
➜ echo ${file}
my important file.txt

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main [?]
➜ rm $file
rm: cannot remove 'my': No such file or directory
rm: cannot remove 'important': No such file or directory
rm: cannot remove 'file.txt': No such file or directory

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main [?]
❯ rm "$file"

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main [?]
➜ ls
notes


-----

Command Substitutions

Command outputs can be captured into variables.


Example:

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main
➜ today=$(date +%Y-%m-%d)

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main
➜ echo "today is $today"
today is 2026-09-16

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main
➜ echo "today is "$today""
today is 2026-09-16

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main
➜ current_dir=$(pwd)

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main
➜ branch=$(git branch --show-current)

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main
➜ echo "Current directory is ${current_dir}" && echo "Current branch is ${branch}"

Current directory is /home/hunter/Projects/lab/Bash
Current branch is main



-----

Special variables

There are special characters that take the various parts of a script.

```sp_var

#!/bin/bash
echo "Script name: $0"
echo "First argument: $1"
echo "All arguments: $@"
echo "Number of arguments: $#"

```

Example:

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main [⇡]
➜ vim sp_var

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main [?⇡] took 1m12s
➜ ./sp_var hello world
-bash: ./sp_var: Permission denied

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main [?⇡]
➜ ./sp_var hello world
Script name: ./sp_var
First argument: hello
All arguments: hello world
Number of arguments: 2

hunter in 🌐 ubuntu in lab/Bash on  main [?⇡]
